        "text": "Blockchain technology does have some limitations, however. Blockchain's immutability comes with a downside when it's necessary to make changes. There aren't many good solutions to this problem, and this can hinder the evolution of a blockchain system. Blockchains use public key cryptography to secure the ownership of value in the system. If a user loses their keys, the value that those keys grant access to becomes inaccessible forever. Blockchains, and more specifically Bitcoin, has been a target of criticism over its high energy consumption. Another limitation to consider is storage. As the size of the blockchain grows, the entry barrier could become higher. What follows is that there would be fewer machines in the distributed system, which may have a detrimental effect. The network's resilience to attacks and exploits could dwindle.",
